  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Logic. 4 players, 2 teams. 24 cards (A-Q of 2 suits). Deal 6 each; arrange ascending. Partner shows you one card privately. Guess opponent card by position+rank. Correct: opponent reveals. Wrong: you reveal one of yours. Can declare all remaining cards at any timeâ€”must be 100% correct or team loses.',
    Player: "Welcome to Logic! Arrange your 6 cards in ascending order. Your partner will show you one of theirsâ€”use this information wisely. Guess your opponents' hidden cards by position and rank. Guess right, they reveal. Guess wrong, you reveal one of yours. When you think you know ALL the hidden cards, declareâ€”but get even one wrong, and your team loses!",
    objective: 'Be the first player to correctly declare the identities of all cards still in play.',
    gameplay: "1. **The Show**: Your partner privately shows you one of their face-down cards. You now know its identity and position. 2. **The Guess**: You must guess the identity of one of your OPPONENTS' face-down cards (Position + Rank). 3. **The Reveal**: If correct: The opponent turns the card face-up permanently. If incorrect: YOU must choose one of your own face-down cards to reveal face-up. 4. **Winning Declaration**: A player can 'Declare' at any time. They must correctly identify EVERY remaining face-down card in the game (teammates and opponents). If they get even one wrong, their team loses immediately.",
    keyRules: [
      'Cards arranged in ascending order left to right.',
      'Partner shows you one card (identity and position).',
      "Guess opponent's card by position and rank.",
      'Correct guess: opponent reveals that card.',
      'Incorrect guess: you must reveal one of your own cards.',
      'Can declare at any time to name all remaining face-down cards.',
      'Declaration must be 100% correct or your team loses.',
    ],
